        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2024",
        "question_text": "<p>According to Boyle's Law, the pressure of a given mass of gas is inversely proportional to its volume at constant temperature. Which of the following equations represents Boyle's Law?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Boyle's Law states that $P \\propto \\frac{1}{V}$ at constant temperature, which can be written as $PV = k$, where $k$ is a constant.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [
            {
                "option_id": "37187",
                "tag": "a",
                "text": "$P_1V_1 = P_2V_2$",
                "is_correct": true
            },
            {
                "option_id": "17243",
                "tag": "b",
                "text": "$\\frac{P_1}{V_1} = \\frac{P_2}{V_2}$",
                "is_correct": false
            },
            {
                "option_id": "95205",
                "tag": "c",
                "text": "$P_1 + V_1 = P_2 + V_2$",
                "is_correct": false
            },
            {
                "option_id": "25657",
                "tag": "d",
                "text": "$\\frac{V_1}{T_1} = \\frac{V_2}{T_2}$",
                "is_correct": false
            }
        ],
